Fix AI replying in the wrong language (e.g. random Chinese)

The language instruction allowed the model to "reply in the same language
the customer is using" with only a weak fallback. On low-signal customer
messages (a product name, a number, an emoji, a one-word greeting) the fast
models guessed a language and drifted to Chinese.

New shared languageRule(): detect language ONLY from the customer's own
words, fall back to the workspace default language (or English) on ambiguity,
and never switch to a language the customer hasn't actually used. Applied to
both suggest-reply and the autonomous auto-responder.

